error: an arm of a match that produces a value must be one expression; found a second statement starting with 'print'
  --> tests/diagnostics/cases/match-arm-second-statement.min:8:13
   |
 8 |             print(problem)
   |             ^^^^^
   = help: a match that produces a value needs one expression in each arm. To leave early from one case, check it as a statement first: `if result is Err(problem) { print(problem); return 1 }`, then read `result.unwrap()`. Otherwise use the match as a statement and assign a binding inside each arm
   = explain: minyar explain E0207
